# Frequently asked questions

## Joining and controls

### Why can I watch but not drive?

Your ticket determines your role. Only a driver ticket for a claimed station can send drive and mechanism frames. Spectators receive the same match snapshots and events, but cannot move a robot. Ask the host to assign or correct your station before the room is locked.

### I rejoined and the field was empty. What should I do?

Reconnect through the same lobby. The first state after a successful reconnect is a complete authoritative baseline; wait for it before judging the field. If the socket repeatedly closes, refresh the page, verify the game-server address configured by the room, and ask the host whether the room was reset or ended.

### Why does the fly camera stop the robot?

An unlocked fly camera uses the keyboard for camera movement, so driver input is intentionally suppressed. Use **Lock camera & drive** to hold the fly camera in place while returning keyboard control to the robot.

### Which gamepad buttons run mechanisms?

The default mapping uses the left bumper for intake, right bumper for outtake, and the top face button for climb. The current controller mapping is shown in the match HUD and can be adjusted from Settings.

## Match and scoring

### Why did my outtake not fire?

The flywheel can accelerate only a ball that has physically reached the outtake. Run the intake first, give the transfer path time to feed a ball forward, and check the robot's stored-ball count.

### Why did the robot slide or fall from the BRACE?

Climbing is physical. The grooved wheels must be aligned around the tube and carry enough normal load for friction to transmit motor torque. Pressing climb only spins the wheels; it does not create an attachment. Reposition, slow down, and establish a clean wheel-to-tube contact.

### Why did a ball not score?

Only active authored scoring volumes count. In the FGC 2026 pack, a WILDFIRE scores when it crosses the correct Suppression Unit target after a robot outtake. A ball touching an inactive target, entering from the wrong path, or merely appearing near the visual model does not create a score.

### Does the timer freeze physics at zero?

No. At the buzzer, player input is disabled while the live physics simulation continues for a short settlement period. This allows a final in-flight ball to finish naturally. The full-screen result overlay then fades in with the finalized score.

## Support

### Why is my invitation code not working?

Codes contain exactly six letters or digits and are single-use. Check the code carefully; a redeemed, revoked, or expired code needs to be replaced by its issuer.

### How do I report a match problem?

Capture the match ID, approximate time, browser console or diagnostics output, and a short description of the expected and observed behavior. For physical issues, include a screenshot or recording with the field and robot visible.

For access, account, or project questions, email [vietnamteamfgc@gmail.com](mailto:vietnamteamfgc@gmail.com). You can also follow [Team Vietnam on Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/TeamVietnamFGC) and [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/teamvietnam.fgc/).

